= Labor Unrest

The mining and metals industry of the Ruhr region is beset by a wave of strikes against cuts to wages and benefits. While Labor minister Rudolf Wissel has arbitrated a deal favorable to the unions. Meanwhile, employers have started a retaliatory lockout to force their workers to accept these cuts. These lock outs are illegal but the state(predictably) has yet to intervene.

- @support_labor: Support the workers in the Reichstag.
- @aid_and_support: Support workers in the Reichstag and the streets.
- @rally_against_spd: We seize the moment to attack the SPD's handling of the unrest.

@support_labor
subtitle: This will alienate the bourgeoisie.
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_kpd += 3*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; inflation += 0.1; economic_growth -= 0.2

We vote with the SPD in the Reichstag to provide support to the workers.

-@ruhr_resolution

@aid_and_support
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_kpd += 2*(1-dissent); workers_kpd += 2*(1-dissent)

We vote with the SPD in the Reichstag to provide support to the workers and give aid to locked out workers. While straining on party finances, it greatly improves our image among the Ruhr workers.

-@ruhr_resolution

@rally_against_spd
choose-if: united_front_maintained == 0
unavailable-subtitle: Or maybe it isn't?
subtitle: This is the SPD's fault.
on-arrival: conciliator_dissent += 5; right_opposition_dissent += 5; workers_spd -= 2; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; spd_relation -= 5; workers_kpd += 2

We attack the SPD for refusing to help the workers aswell as criticising the state's obvious bourgeois bias. They're supposedly socialists, ones in government no less, but can't even use that power to help workers.

-@ruhr_resolution

@ruhr_resolution
title: The dust settles..

The lockout is ended by Minister of the Interior Carl Severing, arbitrating a pay lower than what Wissel granted. The courts later rule in favor of the employeers, declaring arbitration decisions to be inadmissable. The bourgeoisie have unfourtunately won this battle...